---
import Main from '../layouts/Main.astro';
---
<Main title="Explore" description="Probability you can watch move — conditional probability over a shrinking sample space, estimators, expected value and the gambler's fallacy, demonstrated with live card and wheel models." activeNav="explore">

<style>
  .explore-hero {
    padding: 5rem 2rem 3rem;
    max-width: 700px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .explore-hero h1 {
    font-size: 1.8rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: .4rem;
  }
  .explore-hero p { color: var(--txt2); font-size: .95rem; }

  .lede {
    max-width: 700px; margin: 0 auto 2.5rem; padding: 1.1rem 1.3rem;
    background: var(--surf); border: 1px solid var(--bdr);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--teal); border-radius: 8px;
    font-size: .88rem; color: var(--txt2); line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .lede strong { color: var(--txt); }
  .grp {
    max-width: 700px; margin: 3.5rem auto 1rem; padding: 0 2rem;
    font-family: 'Space Mono', monospace; font-size: .65rem; letter-spacing: .16em;
    text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--mut); font-weight: 400;
  }
  .topics {
    max-width: 700px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 2rem 5rem;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(200px, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
  }
  .topic {
    background: var(--surf);
    border: 1px solid var(--bdr);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    text-align: center;
    transition: border-color .2s;
  }
  .topic:hover { border-color: var(--teal); }
  a.topic { cursor: pointer; }
  .topic .icon { font-size: 2rem; margin-bottom: .6rem; display: block; }
  .topic h3 { font-size: .9rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: .2rem; }
  .topic p { font-size: .75rem; color: var(--mut); }
  .soon {
    font-family: 'Space Mono', monospace;
    font-size: .55rem;
    letter-spacing: .1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--amb);
    background: var(--adim);
    border: 1px solid var(--aline);
    padding: .15rem .5rem;
    border-radius: 2px;
    margin-top: .5rem;
    display: inline-block;
  }
</style>

<div class="explore-hero">
  <h1>Probability, Live</h1>
  <p>Textbook probability is static: a fixed deck, a fixed answer. These are the same
     mathematics running in real time on a shrinking, changing sample space &mdash; conditional
     probability, expected value and variance where you can watch the distribution move.
     Plus a few other things that don&rsquo;t fit anywhere else.</p>
</div>

<div class="lede">
  <strong>Why card counting is worth a maths student&rsquo;s attention.</strong> A shoe of cards is a
  finite population sampled <em>without replacement</em>, so every card dealt rewrites the
  distribution for every card still to come. That is the definition of conditional probability,
  and it is unusually easy to see here: the count is nothing more than a running sufficient
  statistic for the composition of what is left. The Hi-Lo count is the crude estimator; exact
  shoe tracking is the full posterior. Watching those two disagree, and by how much, teaches
  more about estimation than a chapter of worked urn problems.
</div>

<div class="topics">
  <a href="/roulette-calculator" class="topic" style="text-decoration:none;">
    <span class="icon">&#127922;</span>
    <h3>Roulette Calculator</h3>
    <p>Independent trials, and why no amount of history changes the next spin &mdash; the
       gambler&rsquo;s fallacy shown with the arithmetic in front of you.</p>
  </a>
  <a href="/blackjack-simulator" class="topic" style="text-decoration:none;">
    <span class="icon">&#127183;</span>
    <h3>Blackjack Simulator</h3>
    <p>A running estimator over a shrinking sample space: Hi-Lo as a sufficient statistic, and
       true count as the correction that makes it comparable across shoe depths.</p>
  </a>
  <a href="/explore/blackjack-engine/" class="topic" style="text-decoration:none;">
    <span class="icon">&#129351;</span>
    <h3>Blackjack Card Counter</h3>
    <p>The exact conditional distribution, not an approximation of it &mdash; every decision
       solved from the cards that remain. Compare it against Hi-Lo to see what the estimator
       throws away.</p>
  </a>
</div>

